      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-01-18_WidnesExaminer_art0011" n="art0011">
        <head>PARR'S BANK, LIMITED. The Report of the Directors.</head>
        <p>PARR'S BANK, LIMITED. The Report of the Directors.</p>
        <p>The report and balance sheet of Parr's Bank, Limited, for the half year ended 31st December last has been issued. The annual ordinary general meeting of the Company will be held at the Cannon-street Hotel, Lon- don, E.C., on Thursday, the 24th that, for the purpose of declaring dividends to be payable on the let Febru- ary and Ist May; electing directors and auditors ; and conducting the ordinary busines of the Company. The directors, in submitting to the shareholders the balance sheet of the bank at 31st December,certified by the auditors, report that the position and prospects of the business continue to be in every way satisfactory. Including £94,329 134 ld brought forward at 30th June, 1900, the net balance of profits, after providing for all bad and doubtful debts, and rebating the current bills at 5 per cent is £259,263 Os sd. From this sum the directors recommend n--a dividend at the rate of 19 per cant per annum for the quarter ended 31st December, 1900, payable, free of income tax, on let February, £69,516 55 ; a bonus of 1 per cent pay- bifree of Income tax, on let February, .914,635 ; aadelvidend at the rate of 19 per cent per annum for the quarter ending 31st March, payable, free of income tax, on lit Mayethe shareholders whose names shall be on the register on 11th April £69,516 sa; the transfer to bank premises account £lO,OOO. total £163,567 104; leaving balance to te carried te next account £5,595 lOs sd, The transfer of the business of the Astiton,Stalybridge, Hyde and Glossop Bank, Limited, bets been successfully completed. Branches of the Bank have been opened at St Leonard, and Stair bridge. and sub-branches at Gate- acre, near Liverpool, and Gorton, Manchester. The Directors who retire at this time by rotation are Mr H B Muir, Mr U C Ross, Mr P Stubs, Sir David Gamble, Bart., C. 8., Mr John Dun, and Mr E W Nis, all of whom are eligible for re•election. The auditors, Messrs Turquand, Youngs, Bishop Az. Clarke, London ; Messrs Stead, Taylor and Stead, Liverpool ; and Messrs Alfred Tongue and Co., Manchester, also retire, and offer thenaseives for re-election.</p>
        <p>Warrington Markets. At the Warrington corn market on Wednesday wheat fetched 33 8d to 3s 10d (70113 to the bushel) ; new oat?, 2s 5d to 21 Od ; flour, best seconds, per 2401 b, 20.5; bran IGid per 201 b. At the Provision Market prices were as follows ;—Fresh butter Is 2d and Is 3d 1,6 d, 7d and Brl per lb ; fresh egg' fowls, 4s to 58 6d per couple; Hug) mutton, 7d to 10d; veal 7d</p>
