      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-01-18_WidnesExaminer_art0031" n="art0031">
        <head>POWER OF SYMPATHY.</head>
        <p>THE POWER OF SYMPATHY.</p>
        <p>(A Trades Union Poem). [ln the labour crisis of the future the federation of trades unions should be able to call out those engaged in every occupation. , A sympathetic strike of this kind would promptly defeat the employers."—A Daily Paper.] The maker of cheap tin trumpets paused in his humble trade, Felt that he had a grievance—knew ho was underpaid, Found that his base employer wouldn't at once consent Even to raise his wages fifty or so per cent. "What ?" cried the agitator, " what, do you still endure Cruelty, greed, oppression—having a certain cure ? Nerve yourself tor a struggle ! Cease to be wail your luck ! Strike ! " said the agitator. The maker of trumpets struck. Promptly the morning papers news of his deed rehearsed, And the mightty heart of Labour with sympathy fairly burst. " Oh," said the railway porter, " label your bloornin'</p>
        <p>bike, -- While the maker of cheap tin -trumpets is driven to go on strike ? Futlow my hocoupatiou while 'e's suff.2rin' wrongs like these? Not," said the railway porter, "if yer arek on yer bonded knees I" "While happy "(so wrote the grocer) " your orders to</p>
        <p>execute, Sympathy is the feature distinguishind man from brute, Noting receipt ot favour, and thanking you for the same— When the maker of cheap tin-trucapets is given his law- ful claim, And his base employer vanquished—then, Madam, with- out delay We'll forward the rice and sugar, as orderel by you to day." " Charge !" cried the gallant leadsr, as be pointed towards the foe ; But the soldiers lo,kad at each aher, and solemnly answered "No! Excuse 118, Str,but they tell Us that otr..r the distant seas A poor old trumpet maker is begging his bit of cheese, And, till they've given biecafreely his proper and lawful Honestly, we assure you, right, we baven't the heart to fight 1" This a journalist told us. Then with a rob of pride Turned to his editor, fknging stylograpli pen aside; "Finish the par.!" he shouted. "alter it as you tare— Sympathy bids ma also join 10 the general strike ! World.</p>
      </div>
