      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-01-18_WidnesExaminer_art0101" n="art0101">
        <head>EDNESDAY —Before Messrs 9 R Armitage (in the chair:,</head>
        <p>EDNESDAY —Before Messrs 9 R Armitage (in the chair:,</p>
        <p>and 3 Ball. DEFRAUDING THE CHESHIRE LINES COMMITTEE.—JOMI I Weaver, 5, Leonard-street, Warrington. was charged with travelling on the Cheshire Lines Railway from Garston to Sankey on the 30th December without previously paying the fare, with intent to defraud—Mr. Simpson prosecuted on behalf of the Cheshire:Lines Committee and stated that the I defendant was found by the special examiners at Sankey on the date in question, to be without a ticket. When asked , for a ticket he said he was a committee's servant employed I lin the works at Warrington as a boiler maker. He was asked I to produce his pass and he said he forgot to bring it with him. He also failed to give satisfactory answers to other questions which were put to hie. Ultimately his name and address were taken and it was ascertained that he was formerly a servant of the committee but was discharged twelve months ago.—A fine of 10s and costs was Imposed. No DIOEIT—John Phythian was fined 2s 61 for falling to have a lighted lam? attached to a vehicle of which he was In charge at 730 p.m. on the 12th inst in Liverpool-road, Sankey. DAMAGING PLOUGHED LAND.—A WORKMAN SUMMONED.— Fred Webb was summoned for committing damage to plough- ed land belonging to Isaac Joseph Howard, at Houghton, to the amount of 3d on the 7th inst. Mr Knowles appeared on behalf of the prosecutor, and after hearing his statement of the facts of the case, which were to the effect that the defend- ant trespassed on his way to work, the Bench ordered defendant to pay the amount of the damages together with the Costs.</p>
        <p>A WOMAN SAVAGELY ASSAULTED AT BUBTONWOOD.—James Haverty was summoned by Mary Marnell for assaulting her at Burtonwood on the 30th December.—Complainant stated that without provocation the defendant seized her by the throat, threw her to the ground and kicked her. When she got up he pushed her into the hedge and her head came into contact with the barbed wires. He then punched her in the face —Defendant was fined 105. and costs with the option of 14 days imprisonment.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-01-18_WidnesExaminer_art0102" n="art0102">
        <head>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT</p>
        <p>ASSOCIATION FOOTBALL LEAGUE --- Pcsition of clubs up to January 12th, 1901 :- IsT DlvisioN. _ .</p>
        <p>Goals.</p>
        <p>P. W. L. D. For Agst. Pt. Trinity Athletic 6.. 4 . 0 .. 2 9 ... 4 ...10 St. Helens L. Fs N.-W Rees 7 ... 3 ... 2 ... 2 9 ... 4 ... 8 Orford Barracks 5 .2.. 2 . 1 5 . 4 ... 5 Penketh St. Mary's Golborne Bees —</p>
        <p>------- 2ND DIVISION. P. W. L. D. For Apt. Pt Warrington Athletic l6 ...I0 ... 4 2 ... 41 ...20 ...22 Stockton Heath l7 ...I0 ... 5 ... 2 ... 40 ...29 ...22 Latchford l7 . 9 .. 6.. 2 ... 38 ...26 ...20 Trinity Athletic Reserve 11 ... 9 1 ... 1 ... 22 8 —.19 Britannia Combination Bewsey All Saints St. Austin's l4 .. 7 .. 5 2 27 ...21 ...I6 St. fdary's Reserve ll ... 6 ... 4 ... 1 ... N ...16 ...13 *Newton St. Peter's Frodsharn Parish Church 12 ... 2 ... 0 ... 19 ...33 ... 4 Walton Warrington Hornets *Pico points deducted for playing an ineligible man.</p>
