        <p>and they corresponded. Ile had had considerable ex• perience in comparing handwritings. P.C. Newsy said that he charged the prisoner the previous night with stealing a post letter containing two £1 orders. His reply was, "I have nothing to say, I am innocent." Prisoner was committed for trial on this charge, bail being refused.</p>
        <p>that Wordsworth conld not be placed in the first rank of RESIGNATION OF THE poets. He could not regard him as a first-class poet in the same sense he would speak of Byron or Shelley. MAYOR'S AUDITOR. Mr G CARRUTHERS alluded to one or two of the familiar spots associated with seine of Wordsworth's poetry. In his love of nature he was forestalltd to a certain extent by Cowper. The characteristics of Woris- worth,his intense love of everything in this world might be found intensified, even in daose poems with regard to animals, in Cowper. But Wordsworth's position was entirely natural, and no man would spend his time in the district he wrote about without having many of the feelings in common with him. Wordsworth had been criticised because of his "awful rubbish," but he (tbe speaker) did not think he had written an thing that could really be said to interfere with his reputation as a poet. It Wordsworth did net found a new religion he gave them many ideals which were almost as good as a new religion. The vote was carried unanimously. Dr NADEN aeknowledeed the compliment and replied to some of the criticisms raised.</p>
