        <p>A FEW TIMELY REMARKS BY pIT TS' S, LONDON-ROAD, MANCHESTER (Just past Station, through Railway Arch). ALSO AT PITTS'S PANTHEON GAYTHORN (Just past Manchester Central Station), THE PROSPEROUS GENERAL FURNISHERS. ON THE THRESHOLD OF A NEW YEAR, the 57th of PITTS'S Business Career, we deem it ad- visable to scan past working in order to draw inspiration and guidance for the future. As space permits but a brief retrospect, we refer only to what has been achieved since our advent in London-road. PITTS'S aspire and persevere, or, in homely language, we aim high and keep pegging at It. This, we believe, is the only royal road to success, the only path to prosperity, the one bee-line for the ambitious. We pursue it now and always have done„ with what results the following shows. First, as regards quality of business, IT MAY INTEREST YOU TO KNOW that we have had the honour of supplying,from London-road,furniture for the office of. HIS GRACE THE DUKE OF DEVONSHIRE. MG., and that we have had the pride and pleasure of executing, from Gaythorn, two separate orders for HIS MAJESTY THE SULTAN OF MOROCCO. A really magnificent lounge suite specially manufactured by PITTS'S, which formed a portion of,the latter orders, was exhibited in our showrooms and gained unstinted praise from those who saw it, whilst it caused unfeigned delight to His Majesty's representatives who had actnally ordered the goods. TN ADDITION TO THE ELITE, we have minis- tered to the requirements of most other grades of society, down to the humble, though necessary, artisan, besides pub. lie and private institutions, corporations, &amp;c.. Ac., and in several instances PITTS'S HAVE F URNISHED THE THIRD GENERATION, having previously supplied the household requisities for the parents and grandparents when they first embarked in married life, and we hope, in the fulness of time to do the like far the fourth and succeeding generations. I MOW AS REGARDS THE QUANTITY OF .1.11 BUSINESS. The great and instantaneous success of ' the Pantheon at Gaythorn, opened in June last, has con- siderably, augmented, PITTs'S already vast turnover, caus- ing the sales for the past six mouths to EXCEED BY A RATE of £20,000 per annum those of the same period in 1896, whilst materially strengthening PITTS'S prestige and enabling us to practically dominate middle-3lass furnishing in the Man Chester locality. No other furnishers in the united Kingdom succes!ully conduct in one town two separate establishments of the magnitude of PITTS'S, each of which is greater than any would-be competitors in this city. WHAT IS THE NET RESULT 7—Well. judging by the ever-increasing support and the numerous press appreciations and unsolicited testimonials ireceived, it quite evident the public generally are thoroughly convinced ' of PITTS'S ability and desire to please and satisfy them, and. that PITTS'S premises, stock, and business are SECOND TO NONE of their kind. But what about the Es. d net result you ask. Sorry we cannot enlighten you, as that is just the little bit we reserve for home consumption. piTTS'S CELEBRATED DOUSES OF TURE, at 151, 22i 28k, 38), 50, 75. 100, 200, up to 1,000 guineas are,in point of Exceilence,Durability and VALUE the VERY BEST OBTAINABLE. They represent a CLEAR SAVING- OF 50 PER CENT as compared with others. Full particulars and NEW ILLUSTRATED FURNISHING GUlDE,containing 700 designs,priced, post free. Cash prices only qnoted ; deferred payments arranged, suiting conveni- ence. DITTS'S PIANOS, CYCLES, BASSI'S ETTES, MAIL! CARTS,LAMPS, CHINA, GLASS, EARTHENWARE, Magnificent Selection. Astounding Value. Well worth inspection. SAMUEL PITTS, MANCHESTER, LONDON-ROAD (Ardwiek and Longsight Cars); GAYTHORN (all City-road Cars pass the door). Established 1845. National Telephone, 1,124 BUSINESS HOURS 8 to 7 SATURDAYS, 8 to 9</p>
